[agent] I completed what the interface allows and hit a hard capability gap for the rest. Here is the faithful outcome.
[agent] ## What I did (through the allowed interface: `bq` + GA `gcloud ai/…`)
[agent] - **Loaded all six increments** into a BigQuery-backed offline feature table `incremental0872b7` inside `GCP_BQ_DATASET` (`mlpab_mlpab4af340`), with the documented schema (`row_id` STRING key, `account_id`, `event_time` INT64 epoch-ms, `amount`, `category`). Verified: **631 rows, 631 distinct `row_id`** (= 637 CSV lines − 6 headers), `event_time` range 1772409600000–1772927700000.
[agent] - Created `incremental0872b7_staging` (same schema) as the landing table a daily job would MERGE from.
[agent] - Wrote the named deliverable `submission/answers.json` → `{"job_name": "incrementaljob0872b7"}`.
[agent] ## Capabilities the interface is missing (could not complete)
[agent] The GA `gcloud ai` surface exposes only: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`. It has **no Vertex AI Feature Store commands** and **no ingestion scheduler**:
[agent] 1. **Online / low-latency serving + feature-group registration.** The Vertex AI Feature Store commands (`feature-groups`, `feature-online-stores`, `feature-views` — the resources that register a feature table with a record key/event-time and distinguish online vs. offline) exist only under `gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai`. Those top-level tracks are hard-blocked by the sandbox (`DENIED: gcloud beta … is off-interface`). GA `gcloud ai` cannot create them, and `gcloud bigtable` (the other online path) is not in the allowlist either. So the offline data landed in BigQuery, but I could not register a feature group or stand up an online store.
[agent] 2. **Recurring daily ingestion job with an attached schedule.** GA `gcloud ai` has no schedule/cron for `custom-jobs` (one-shot only); Vertex Pipeline/Feature-View sync schedules are beta-only (blocked). I attempted the one remaining allowed path — a **BigQuery scheduled query** (`bq mk --transfer_config … --schedule="every 24 hours"`, a real recurring platform job with the schedule attached). It cannot be created here: the user-credential path demands interactive OAuth `version_info` (no refresh token — the identity is an impersonated SA with only an access token), and the `--service_account_name` path fails because the BigQuery Data Transfer service agent needs a `roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator` binding on `mlpab-sa@…`, which requires `gcloud iam …` — also outside the allowlist.
[agent] The `model-monitoring-jobs --monitoring-frequency` flag is the only GA recurring schedule in `gcloud ai`, but it monitors a deployed model endpoint for drift — it is not an increment-ingestion pipeline and needs an endpoint/model unrelated to this task, so I did not fabricate one just to occupy the name.
[agent] **Net:** offline increments are fully loaded into the BigQuery-backed store; the online feature store and the recurring scheduled ingestion pipeline are not reachable through the GA `gcloud ai` + `bq` interface as configured (the required surfaces are beta/alpha-only or need blocked `gcloud iam` bindings).
